Three verdict-shaping points:

1. The novelty is in the functional, not the numbers. All four agents converged on this: peak-residual-nnz-minimized-over-orderings is not a named quantity anywhere found. The values (10, 26) are computations downstream of the new definition. The nearest literature — Boyer–Dumas–Pernet–Zhou scheduling, classical pebbling (Sethi 1975, Hopcroft–Paul–Valiant 1977) — counts implementation temporaries on a computation DAG, a genuinely different object even for the same algorithm.
2. Two import channels surfaced. Rival–Zaguia (Order, 1985: antichain cutsets of Boolean lattices = level sets) gives the combinatorial skeleton behind why level cuts block, but not the weighted equality C2 claims — the gap being that H_t isn't an antichain and f is non-monotone. Wei's generalized Hamming weights (1991) is a structural analogue for the w_min profile with existing duality/monotonicity machinery. Both are candidate tooling for attacking C2–C4, not threats to novelty.
3. Residual risk sits on C2/C3. Both are "no prior art found" at only medium confidence — a weighted min-max theorem on Boolean lattices could live in extremal combinatorics the quick pass didn't reach, and the literature agent didn't read BDPZ full-text. These were quick sweeps by design; if any of this heads toward a manuscript, the C2/C3 neighborhood and the "one-shpergraph" framing deserve adeep sweep.
